FileSystemWatcher.OSX.cs is only compiled on the macOS profile, which
upstream always built with csc/Roslyn; on big-endian hosts the build
uses mcs, which stops at C# 7.x, never implemented local functions,
and binds span.Equals(string, StringComparison) to the inapplicable
static object.Equals instead of falling through to MemoryExtensions.
Downgrade the C# 8 constructs ('is null', using-declaration and
pattern-based using on a ref struct -> try/finally, [^1]), hoist the
ParseEvent local function into a private static method and call
MemoryExtensions.Equals explicitly.  No functional change.
